% A fermata on one note of a chord, as in [Hce] or [cHe], lengthens the
% whole chord, as H[ce] does.  abc2midi lengthened only that note: the
% chord then had unequal notes, an error with -Werror, and the fermata was
% not played when the note was not the first one of the chord, when the
% chord had a length after its ], or on the other notes of a chord that
% starts with a rest.  Tune 2 plays chords with %%MIDI fermatafixed, which
% lengthens them by one unit length, here an eighth note.
X:1
T:Fermatas in chords
C:abc2midi test
M:4/4
L:1/4
Q:1/4=120
K:C
[Hce] c d e |[cHe] c d e |[Hce]2 c d |[cHe]2 c d |
[Hz e] c d e |(3[cHe]cc d e |[c!fermata!eg] c d e |H[ce] c d e |]

X:2
T:Fermatas in chords, fermatafixed
C:abc2midi test
M:4/4
L:1/8
Q:1/4=120
K:C
%%MIDI fermatafixed
[Hc2e2] c2 d2 e2 |[c2He2] c2 d2 e2 |H[c2e2] c2 d2 e2 |Hc2 c2 d2 e2 |]
